; This repo keeps native modules (better-sqlite3) out of the root
; node_modules on purpose — they're installed only inside release/app/
; (see .erb/scripts/check-native-dep.js), rebuilt there for Electron's ABI
; rather than the host Node's. Modern npm auto-installs optional peer
; dependencies by default, which pulls drizzle-orm's optional `better-sqlite3`
; peer straight into the root install and trips that check.
;
; omit=peer (not omit=optional!) is the precise fix: it stops npm's
; auto-install-peer-deps behavior without touching real optionalDependencies
; entries elsewhere in the tree (e.g. lightningcss's per-platform native
; binaries, needed for the Tailwind v4 PostCSS build to work at all —
; omit=optional would silently break that).
omit=peer
